.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
node_modules/
.claude/

# editor/tooling backups; these were untracked cruft that a blanket
# `git add -A` swept into the relaunch branch
*.bak
*.orig

# Working notes and audits. This repo is PUBLIC and serves middleton.io, so a
# candid review of Kevin's own record ("four months as co-founder is a red
# flag", "I will probe the short tenures hard") must never reach it: useful to
# him, damaging if a recruiter found it on his own domain. Same `git add -A`
# hazard as the backups above, higher cost.
*-REVIEW-*.md
*-AUDIT-*.md
notes/
_working/

# Local-only explainers and decks. Public repo: these must never ship.
_*.html

# 53MB of full-size blog sources that GitHub Pages was serving publicly while
# nothing linked them. Kept locally by tools/blog-generate.mjs; the README stays
# tracked so the folder explains itself on GitHub. See that README before
# assuming an original still exists: CI-run optimizations cannot preserve one.
blog/images/_originals/*
!blog/images/_originals/README.md
